1. Difference between Frontend, Backend, and Full-Stack Development
----------------------------------------------------------

Frontend Development:
Frontend is the part of a website that users can see and interact with. It includes the design, layout, buttons, menus, images, and everything visible on the screen.

Technologies Used:
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript

Example:
When we open Amazon, the homepage, search bar, product images, and navigation menu are all part of the frontend.

Backend Development:
Backend is the part of a website that works behind the scenes. It manages the server, database, business logic, and user authentication.

Technologies Used:
- Java
- Python
- Node.js
- PHP
- MySQL
- MongoDB

Example:
When a user logs into Amazon, the backend checks the username and password from the database and allows access if the details are correct.

Full-Stack Development:
A Full-Stack Developer works on both the frontend and backend. They can build an entire web application from the user interface to the database.

Example:
A developer building a complete e-commerce website like Amazon is working as a full-stack developer.

